    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Lars Onsager (1949) and, independently, Richard Feynman (1955) proposed that frictionless superfluid helium-4 can only rotate by threading itself with discrete vortex lines, each carrying exactly one quantum of circulation,">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/fields/quantum_fields/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_superfluid_vortex_quantization_thumb.png
